# Scenario 045 — Academic integrity review: governance, memory, reject, human decision
/reset
yes
/enterprise
1
Rimu University Integrity
Uphold academic integrity fairly, with a person accountable for every finding.
skip
/function
1
Integrity Review
Frame academic-integrity questions as fair process and route findings to an accountable panel chair.
skip
/add-human-worker
Panel Chair
1
skip
/function start "Integrity Review"
@timeout 240
@staff /staff
/governance policy add "Integrity analysis requires chair sign-off" --effect require-approval --capability "analysis"
/memory add "Never identify a real student or make a finding; frame process, evidence standards, and appeal rights, and require a human panel for every finding." --scope "Integrity Review"
/task
1
Analyse, using a fully synthetic and anonymised example only, how a suspected-collusion case should be handled as fair process: evidence standards, the student's right to respond, proportionality, appeal rights, and why a panel must decide. Do not make a finding or identify anyone.
1
@wait 20
@cap TASK_ID {(task-[0-9]+)}
/tasks
@wait 8
/approval-status {{TASK_ID}}
/reject {{TASK_ID}} "Example includes identifying details; reframe as anonymised process before analysis."
/task
1
Revised analysis, fully synthetic and anonymised: analyse only the fair-process steps, evidence standards, right to respond, proportionality, and appeal rights, and the point a panel must decide. No identities, no finding.
1
@wait 20
@cap TASK2 {(task-[0-9]+)}
/tasks
@wait 8
/approve {{TASK2}}
@wait 55
/task inspect {{TASK2}}
@cap HTASK {(human-task-[0-9]+)}
/create-human-task "Process decision" "Decide the evidence standard and procedural safeguards a hearing requires, and how appeal rights are communicated. Do not make a finding."
/complete-human-task {{HTASK}} "Require a documented evidence standard, the student's right to respond, and a written appeal path before any hearing. Planning only." --as "Panel Chair"
/human-task {{HTASK}}
/timeline
